I've written two task files and the issue responses, and committed them as 009afe80. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so I had to force-add the files, as earlier sessions did.

• **Task 1 (#963, evolve):** Two compact-thrash tests share one global counter and sometimes fail when run in parallel. That can make the evolve gate revert a correct task. The plan is to have the counter logic take the counter as an argument, so each test uses its own copy while production code stays the same. The check is 20 filtered test runs in a loop, with the real pass count reported. Work is committed before any long cargo run.
• **Task 2 (#964, product):** The warning for setting `max_tokens` above the model's limit never printed on the Anthropic path. The task starts by finding out why and committing that finding before any code changes. It then fixes two things in one diff: the missing warning, and the limit it compares against. Fixing only the first would make it warn wrongly on this repo's correct setting of 128000. If yoagent doesn't expose the model's real maximum, the warning is switched off for those models instead of using the wrong number.
• **Issue responses:**
  • Close #742, which was already fixed by 8d1f0ff3.
  • Defer #958.
  • Leave #959 and #960 open without comment. Those sessions sent the wrong model id and then an over-limit max_tokens to the provider, so every call failed and nothing landed. The config is fixed now, so the tasks themselves weren't the problem.

